A||N||3||Bigfieroman||Exhaust manifold gaskets+bolts?||||1||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||10-05-2001||02:57 PM||||Does anyone know where I can get inexpensive exhause gaskets, and/or does anyone have an recommendation on what to use for bolts for the manifolds?  I have been told that the standard ones are changed by the heat and become brittle.  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>87 GT Automatic, Beretta GTZ Wheels, Kuhmo Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Poly cradle bushings.<BR>Future mods: Complete suspension redux w/anti-bumpsteer, all poly, rear swaybar, KYBs, Ground Control Coilovers, Street Dreams lowering spindles, plus exterior redux, w/window and quater panel scoops, Kid Danger air dam, 1fst2m6 style hood vent, 7" taller wing stantions, and black w/ silver racing stripes paint.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic_5.JPG">   <P>3800 S/C after all that!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||10-05-2001||04:56 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012117.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012117.html</A><P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011068.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011068.html</A>  <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||2birds||10-05-2001||10:43 PM||||I got stainless bolts, flatwashers, and lockwashers from Lowe's.  8 X 1.25, not sure about the length, but I got ones that were just a shade longer than the originals.<BR>I installed them on all six spots on both manifolds.  I modified the semi-flat front heat shield by cutting the upper half of the port holes off, so it can be mounted on the outside of the manifold flanges, instead of against the head face. I didn't have to modify the curved front heat shield at all.<BR>Use plenty of anti-sieze on the threads, and clean the threads with a tap prior to assembly.  I torqued them to the factory specs.<BR>I removed the first one I did after six months of operation, and had no trouble with leaks or bolt breakage.  <BR>The Fel-Pro gaskets are probably the best you'll get, at $25, unless the Camaro gaskets mentioned in the above threads work fine.  For a few extra bucks, I got the Fiero gaskets.  Nothing sucks worse than having to do Fiero exhaust gaskets twice. <P>Get plenty of Penetrating fluid and soak them all for a few days before you start.  I did the front head last spring, and didn't break any bolts.  Only took a couple of hours to do.  I already had two broken bolts on the rear, so I ended up removing the head to get one of them removed at a machine shop (one came out easily).  A $10 job (already had the extra gasket, just needed the new hardware) turned into over $200 by the time I bought the gasket set and new head bolts($120) and paid the shop to rebuild the heads, since they were off.  Doesn't burn oil anymore, though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-06-2001||01:10 PM||||everything 2 birds said. Use cheap gaskets and youll be doing them again soo. Felpro is the best.||||reg||1
